  "semantic_repairs": [
    "Mask the actual strided loads; do not dereference inactive/invalid left or right lanes.",
    "Apply second-row upper clamp too.",
    "Explicit canonical NaN propagation through actual checked ordinary helpers.",
    "Odd right absent taps skip FMA entirely by true _mu accumulator-preserving masked FMA; left padding still computes0*weight.",
    "Use local0..3 uint32 lane comparisons plus uint64 global index/address arithmetic; no INT32 dimension cut.",
    "Store row1 before row0 so clipped final row is overwritten by the valid row0, retaining lane0..3 final-channel aliases."
  ],
  "compatibility_changes": [
    "NEON three vertical FMAs extracted to4 ordinary pointer-borrow helpers with original per-accumulator operand/lane/order trace.",
    "NEON low/high selection plus2lane store uses2 ordinary checked pointer-borrow helpers; original row/channel write order retained.",
    "RVV scalar-copy classifier avoids pinned QCP syntactic self-comparison issue; exact binary32 copy body checked.",
    "RVV pure mask comparison/load temporaries made explicit for readonly borrowed record views; scalar reads use actual checked reader.",
    "NEON219 caches original five row bases and calls ordinary pixel27 while retaining channel/row/width cursors and original store order.",
    "RVV162 calls eight ordinary pixel9 wrappers, each doing nine ordered ordinary rows_fma3 calls; each accumulator retains dx,ci,ky27 order and packed112-block lane addresses. Global readonly load/inter-accumulator schedule changes are explicit.",
    "Width invariants use raw logical Z output cursors at one-past2^64; actual uint64 updates retain mod2^64. This is annotation-only, no new domain restriction or C repair."
  ],
  "domain": {
    "dimensions": "uint64 values bounded only by explicit valid nonwrapping input/zero/weights/params/output footprints; positive H/W/channels, top0..1,0<=start<end with2*(end-1)+1-top<H. No arbitrary32bit or finite/ordered-float restriction.",
